  "visual_differences": {
    "all": "The native HUD shows the actual weekdays and uses different type metrics, alignment, widths and trust bar styling. The same locked choices, response text, reputation sources and tones are shown.",
    "j01_j02_j05_j09": "The active gate and player markers, map outlines, lantern shading, grid and label styling differ. Live bar sizing and position change how much of the canal label is covered. The inherited Make up Dhuhr action remains visible. The j02 gate bar wraps below navigation. The j05 and j09 prayer buttons shift above the gate bar. The comparison excludes the transient Asr call per the spec.",
    "j03_j04_j06_j07_j08_j10_j11_j12": "The camera frames the existing placeholder lane leading away from the Gate of Trust, with simple block buildings, a blue sky and a plain ground plane. The masters show a furnished storefront, tiled street, hanging lanterns and a distant arch. The native panels differ in opacity, edge treatment, line wrapping, type spacing, vertical spacing and button widths. The reputation panel also differs in rule contrast and padding.",
    "j10_j11_j12": "The live wallet follows purchases across calendar days, showing 238, 278 and 398 coins. Each master shows a 198-coin fixture. Trust is 45, 40 and 30 respectively in both."
  },
  "pre_release_scholar_review": "Pending under OA-AIOS-432. LOCK 13 §1 cites Quran 2:188 as the design reference for knowingly buying and profiting from someone else's stolen property. Review this portrayal and notifying the owner before public release. DOC-TFG-0320 has no dedicated LOCK 13 row."
